ate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{y}^{2}}^{{y}^{2}+1}y\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[{\\int }_{2{y}^{2}}^{{y}^{2}+1}\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[\\,x\\,]_{2{y}^{2}}^{{y}^{2}+1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y({y}^{2}+1-2{y}^{2})dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-{y}^{3})\\,dy & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332732 13194139535130 true] [17592186332731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332733 13194139535130 true] [17592186332731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332734 13194139535130 true] [17592186332731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332735 13194139535130 true] [17592186332731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332736 13194139535130 true] [17592186332731 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535130 true] [17592186332731 1041 "selection" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332731 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332734 13194139535130 true] [17592186332731 1110 #uuid "0e9b8828-4a18-5a98-a51e-db91abf63004" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332732 1034 "\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332732 1111 #uuid "327c164b-7f45-55af-b466-bc9ff6cf052a" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332733 1034 "2" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332733 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332733 1111 #uuid "9ffd597e-f8d4-5ec2-93f1-0a20dab32d11" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332734 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332734 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332734 1111 #uuid "444fac14-f20e-5218-b051-c8c326242701" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332735 1034 "4" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332735 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332735 1111 #uuid "d0d14262-dd20-5cfa-a9f8-6b9a9a7ad393" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332736 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332736 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332736 1111 #uuid "f6281426-a22c-56a4-b7cd-d229021e250e" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332737 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332738 13194139535130 true] [17592186332737 1089 "q-132531" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332737 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535130 true] [17592186332737 1100 "Calculate ${∬}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,dA,$ where $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2}}.$" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332737 1113 #uuid "b686fe8e-540c-5e6e-855f-cc2825f800a7" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332737 1145 "The integral is defined over a type II region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2}}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}{x}^{2}\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}(\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{6}-0)dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{5}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{5}\\,dy & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{5}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[\\frac{1}{6}{y}^{6}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{32}{3}-\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{21}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332739 13194139535130 true] [17592186332738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332740 13194139535130 true] [17592186332738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332741 13194139535130 true] [17592186332738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332742 13194139535130 true] [17592186332738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332743 13194139535130 true] [17592186332738 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535130 true] [17592186332738 1041 "selection" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332738 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332739 13194139535130 true] [17592186332738 1110 #uuid "ae60d52d-9b12-5be9-bf60-0895f7fb9630" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332739 1034 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332739 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332739 1111 #uuid "17b234b1-8ffc-5360-9b5e-785ffd382aee" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332740 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332740 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332740 1111 #uuid "563a7936-6784-57ac-87a6-ba67f7c55bde" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332741 1034 "8" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332741 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332741 1111 #uuid "51ba1e79-03e1-55ed-9700-630c49339e1d" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332742 1034 "4" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332742 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332742 1111 #uuid "ae1521a1-2e01-5da1-972d-4a0cf33595a1" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332743 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332743 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332743 1111 #uuid "cdcaecb2-46b2-5639-ba48-d4c2a6a4feb8" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332744 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332745 13194139535130 true] [17592186332744 1089 "q-132562" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332744 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535130 true] [17592186332744 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/d5f54020da277980a58151bf2a85911365e67ecae6832881e03ac8b9b6431e6a.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}4x\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D$ is the region enclosed between the curves $16{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16$ and $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16,$ above the $x$-axis, as shown in the picture." 13194139535130 true] [17592186332744 1113 #uuid "4f1f896d-423d-5f07-bb8f-0a0deac07744" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332744 1145 "Notice that $D$ is a type II region. Since $x\\ge 0,$ we obtain the following equations in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{4-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}} & =\\sqrt{4-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}} \\\\ 1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =4-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}{y}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =16 \\\\ y & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our region lies above the $x$-axis, the $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 4.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/d8b8b05e9004f6b25f635e9c39421a8e8e27831a26a22273cf88572df89ffc45.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}4x\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/16}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}/4}}\\,4x\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/16}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}/4}}\\,4x\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}2[{\\int }_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/16}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}/4}}\\,2x\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\,2{[\\,{x}^{2}\\,]}_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/16}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}/4}}\\text{ }dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\,2[4-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-(1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16})]dy \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\,[3-\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{2}]dy \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\,(1-\\frac{1}{16}{y}^{2})dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\,(1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16})dy & =6{[y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{48}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =6(4-\\frac{64}{48}) \\\\  & =6(4-\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332746 13194139535130 true] [17592186332745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332747 13194139535130 true] [17592186332745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332748 13194139535130 true] [17592186332745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332749 13194139535130 true] [17592186332745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332750 13194139535130 true] [17592186332745 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535130 true] [17592186332745 1041 "selection" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332745 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332747 13194139535130 true] [17592186332745 1110 #uuid "c32b5e54-42da-531c-b5b3-821a6d967b9e" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332746 1034 "\\frac{16}{3}" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332746 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332746 1111 #uuid "2758e88f-d1df-5ec6-840f-df02d615ad30" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332747 1034 "16" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332747 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332747 1111 #uuid "cef645cc-499c-57d9-9907-f7d9e4df8858" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332748 1034 "8" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332748 1111 #uuid "cac34dfe-54b3-5c46-9881-eaa692a22f2f" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332749 1034 "\\frac{8}{3}" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332749 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332749 1111 #uuid "392ea7d1-3a92-5a9f-b538-070778a2527b" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332750 1034 "4" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332750 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332750 1111 #uuid "3d8dc75d-93a5-5526-97b2-4b22a8aefdf0" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332751 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332752 13194139535130 true] [17592186332751 1089 "q-37996" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332751 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535130 true] [17592186332751 1100 "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}(1-xy)\\,dx\\,dy=$" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332751 1113 #uuid "9c5423a0-a399-5841-a575-289a1476314b" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332751 1145 "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}(1-xy)\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}(1-xy)\\,dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[x-\\frac{y{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{{y}^{2}}^{y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2}-({y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{5}}{2}))\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2}-{y}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{5}}{2})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2}-{y}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{5}}{2})\\,dy & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{8}-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{6}}{12}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{12}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332753 13194139535130 true] [17592186332752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332754 13194139535130 true] [17592186332752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332755 13194139535130 true] [17592186332752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332756 13194139535130 true] [17592186332752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332757 13194139535130 true] [17592186332752 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535130 true] [17592186332752 1041 "selection" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332752 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332755 13194139535130 true] [17592186332752 1110 #uuid "7911ff55-b633-5c4a-a16a-c106f9006227" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332753 1034 "\\pi -\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332753 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332753 1111 #uuid "0db3bbd6-fb95-526a-980f-021c74948e6d" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332754 1034 "-\\frac{1}{12}" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332754 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332754 1111 #uuid "3faf5f38-2b8a-52c9-bef0-38aa6c7f36a2" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332755 1034 "\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332755 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332755 1111 #uuid "ed7f1485-131c-5911-a020-8c7d15975be7" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332756 1034 "-\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332756 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332756 1111 #uuid "974bbd31-56fb-5e5e-8987-917051a23239" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332757 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332757 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332757 1111 #uuid "6a4889b1-c565-57d9-a289-b4047eeffc57" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332758 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332759 13194139535130 true] [17592186332758 1089 "q-40680" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332758 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535130 true] [17592186332758 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/a135b0766239bcd6e9cacc324572486e66e1c859ecd28a4d59ef7795cc511ed4.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}xy\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D$ is the region enclosed between the curves ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ and $x=0,$ above the $x$-axis and below the line $y=1,$ as shown in the picture." 13194139535130 true] [17592186332758 1113 #uuid "7a5b3321-cf12-51db-a631-dd5473f67f10" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332758 1145 "Notice that $D$ is a type II region. Since $x\\ge 0,$ we obtain the following equations in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}} \\\\ x=0 & \\,⟹\\,x=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 4-{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the $x$-axis and below the line $y=1,$ the $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/373286c03cc595535a7f04987e7454be2fac547d769341343f05ea67ee0b001d.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}xy\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,xy\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,xy\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,xy\\,dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,{[\\,\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}y\\,]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\text{ }dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\frac{1}{2}(4-{y}^{2})ydy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\frac{1}{2}(4y-{y}^{3})dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\frac{1}{2}(4y-{y}^{3})dy & ={[\\frac{1}{2}(2{y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4})]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2-\\frac{1}{4})-\\frac{1}{2}(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332759 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332760 13194139535130 true] [17592186332759 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332761 13194139535130 true] [17592186332759 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332762 13194139535130