_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{3-(y-3)^{2}}^{(y-3)^{2}+4}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{3-(y-3)^{2}}^{(y-3)^{2}+4}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332773 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332774 13194139535130 true] [17592186332773 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332775 13194139535130 true] [17592186332773 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332776 13194139535130 true] [17592186332773 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332777 13194139535130 true] [17592186332773 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332778 13194139535130 true] [17592186332773 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535130 true] [17592186332773 1041 "selection" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332773 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332778 13194139535130 true] [17592186332773 1110 #uuid "8d4a7495-4d32-549a-9853-9ea81c81c0f9" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332774 1034 "{\\int }_{3-(y-3)^{2}}^{(y-3)^{2}+4}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332774 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332774 1111 #uuid "ddec68e4-d6c4-5393-bf36-c522c9d3d1da" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332775 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{(y-3)^{2}+4}^{3-(y-3)^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332775 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332775 1111 #uuid "38541ad2-d5ec-5364-9748-b3de88135016" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332776 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{(y-3)^{2}+4}[{\\int }_{3}^{3-(y-3)^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332776 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332776 1111 #uuid "fa367df2-84c3-58af-8655-6c84c5620c4b" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332777 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{3-(y-3)^{2}}[{\\int }_{3}^{(y-4)^{2}+4}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332777 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332777 1111 #uuid "3995f3d4-28f7-57ca-ba3d-3efb139b50af" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332778 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{3-(y-3)^{2}}^{(y-3)^{2}+4}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332778 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332778 1111 #uuid "c2e9f529-3cbd-58ca-a67f-8e4ef0c98df9" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332779 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332780 13194139535130 true] [17592186332779 1089 "q-81260" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332779 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535130 true] [17592186332779 1100 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed between the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=\\sqrt{x-2}$ from $y=0$ to $y=1.$ What is ${∬}_{D}\\frac{xy}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dA$ expressed as a repeated integral?" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332779 1113 #uuid "9f0dcf3b-fd2c-5538-bc97-3c2c49455a71" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332779 1145 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=\\sqrt{x-2}$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{y} \\\\ y=\\sqrt{x-2} & \\,⟹\\,x={y}^{2}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/bb3249a9580e754c4ef9c33239c2a51a9b57ca9032a6acbeef7bbc532b2d4345.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\sqrt{y}\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{xy}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y}}^{{y}^{2}+2}\\frac{xy}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332781 13194139535130 true] [17592186332780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332782 13194139535130 true] [17592186332780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332783 13194139535130 true] [17592186332780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332784 13194139535130 true] [17592186332780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332785 13194139535130 true] [17592186332780 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535130 true] [17592186332780 1041 "selection" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332780 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332783 13194139535130 true] [17592186332780 1110 #uuid "90519ca9-201c-56ba-9ed7-2533133c0a0b" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332781 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}+2}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{y}}\\frac{xy}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332781 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332781 1111 #uuid "3d44c874-2999-549d-88fe-5515e5b98c7c" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332782 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}{\\int }_{1}^{{y}^{2}+2}\\frac{xy}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332782 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332782 1111 #uuid "f35d13dc-cb15-5954-a279-5e491440e715" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332783 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y}}^{{y}^{2}+2}\\frac{xy}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332783 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332783 1111 #uuid "d48ba639-3036-5f09-845b-fdc141700694" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332784 1034 "{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y}}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}+2}\\frac{xy}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332784 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332784 1111 #uuid "7cab6828-6212-5c15-b5b1-7c2b7d593b79" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332785 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}+2}^{\\sqrt{y}}\\frac{xy}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332785 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535130 true] [17592186332785 1111 #uuid "e1cf699a-266a-5603-a487-7ae6a8000841" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332786 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332787 13194139535130 true] [17592186332786 1089 "q-81291" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332786 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535130 true] [17592186332786 1100 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed between the curves $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ where $x>0,$ and $y=\\frac{x}{2},$ below the line $y=2.$ What is ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA\\,$ expressed as a repeated integral?" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332786 1113 #uuid "37207123-75ea-50cb-aebf-4dad083ae03c" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332786 1145 "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/2209e57f8cbe84ccf2f930c5cd3004ff5009dfb72f3e4b3262517cf9b8f2b119.png)\n\nWe need to represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $y=\\frac{x}{2}$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=\\frac{1}{x} & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ y=\\frac{x}{2} & \\,⟹\\,x=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y} & =2y \\\\ 2y-\\frac{1}{y} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2{y}^{2}-1}{y} & =0 \\\\ 2{y}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies in the first quadrant below the line $y=2$ the $y$-limits are \n$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\le y\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/1b03741537734087836c22dbb40e2e188825bade657cff129374efe1596bcb3c.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\frac{1}{y}\\le x\\le 2y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/2}^{2}{\\int }_{1/y}^{2y}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535130 true] [17592186332787 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332788 13194139535130 true] [17592186332787 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332789 13194139535130 true] [17592186332787 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332790 13194139535130 true] [17592186332787 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332791 13194139535130 